<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Vascones</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 75 BCE (approx.) · capital Pompaelo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The people of Navarre and ancestors of the Basques, whose lands held Pompey's foundation of Pompaelo, modern Pamplona.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Vascones lived in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, roughly modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> and parts of Aragon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rioja-spain">La Rioja</a>, by the 3rd century BCE. They probably spoke an early form of Basque, related to Aquitanian across the mountains.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in hill towns and villages, farming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> plain and herding in the mountains. Their towns included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calagurris">Calagurris</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pompaelo</a>, and they minted coins with Iberian-script legends. They had no single ruler and were organised in local communities.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the winter of 75 to 74 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> camped in their territory, giving his name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pompaelo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calagurris">Calagurris</a> backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-sertorius">Sertorius</a> and fell in 72 BCE after a famous siege. The Vascones were absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, but their language survived and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-navarre">Kingdom of Navarre</a> arose in their land.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 300 BCE – 75 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:4.48%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 75 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pompaelo</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Basque</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vasconians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-188&amp;focus=vascones" aria-label="Vascones on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4640 657 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vascones lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4960 913L5031 967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4960 913h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4960 913h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pompaelo. <a href="/atlas?year=-188&amp;focus=vascones">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
